; Bank $02 -- sound engine. Entry: the main loop pages in this bank and calls
; SoundRunFrame ($556A) once per frame. Backbone (verified by tracing):
;   SoundRunFrame  -- tempo gate ($cb6f frame-skip, $cb70 tick-repeat) -> run SoundTick N times
;   SoundTick      -- one tick: SoundStepAllChannels then SoundUpdateAllChannels
;   SoundStepAllChannels  -- SoundProcessChannel for each active channel (order WAV,PU1,PU2,NOI):
;                          advance phrase via channel cursors, read note/instrument/command,
;                          run the per-tick FX command (SoundDispatchCommand)
;   SoundUpdateAllChannels -- SoundUpdateChannel per channel: write GB sound regs / run tables
; Channels: hSoundChannel ($FF8B) 0-3 = PU1/PU2/WAV/NOI -> rAUD1/2/3/4; KIT plays on WAV.
; Per-channel state is a struct-of-arrays at $C0xx-$C3xx (see constants/ram.inc wChan*);
; working read-cursors are 16-bit ptrs whose low bytes live at $C8xx (SoundInitializeStatePointers
; sets them to channel 0, SoundAdvanceStatePointers steps to the next channel).
494D SoundProcessChannel        ; per-channel sound tick (channel = hSoundChannel); called per active channel
49B7 SoundNoteToPeriod          ; e = the channel (hSoundChannel): wChannelFrequency[ch] = wNotePeriods[note + wNoteTranspose - 1]
4C2D SoundAdvanceChannelCursors ; advance the 3 phrase cursors (note/cmd, cmdval, instr) by c; de = hSoundChannel * 2, their index
4AA3 SoundWriteChannelFrequency ; write the current channel's frequency to rAUDxLOW/HIGH each tick (no retrigger; P/L/V pitch)
; --- Note trigger: write the GB sound regs to start a note on the current channel
6007 SoundTriggerNote           ; dispatch by hSoundChannel to the per-voice trigger below
604B SoundTriggerPu1            ; PU1 note-on: rAUD1 sweep/env/freq + trigger
6091 SoundTriggerPu2            ; PU2 note-on: rAUD2 env/freq + trigger
60D1 SoundTriggerWav            ; WAV note-on: rAUD3 level/freq + trigger
6014 SoundTriggerNoi            ; NOI note-on: rAUD4 len/env/poly + trigger
5151 SoundReadChannelCursor     ; hl = an array's base: -> e = the byte under channel hSoundChannel's 16-bit cursor in it; SRAM-guarded
485A SoundInitializeStatePointers ; set $C8xx to the low-bytes of the engine's $C1xx state ptrs
; --- Note-on: load instrument from SRAM into wCurrentInstrument, set up channel shadows -
5934 SoundSetupChannel          ; dispatch by hSoundChannel to the per-channel setup block below
5942 SoundSetupPu1              ; PU1: stage wCurrentInstrument -> sweep/env/duty/freq shadows + trigger
5A27 SoundSetupPu2              ; PU2: stage wCurrentInstrument -> env/duty/freq shadows + trigger
5B0C SoundSetupWav              ; WAV/KIT: stage wCurrentInstrument -> wave level/freq shadows + trigger
5DB2 SoundSetupNoi              ; NOI: stage wCurrentInstrument -> env/poly shadows + trigger
4F33 FillChannel8               ; write a to the 8 bytes from hl, -> hl past them (clears a per-channel 16-bit array)
4F37 FillChannel4               ; write a to the 4 bytes from hl, -> hl past them (clears a per-channel [4] array)
; --- Table macro playback (per-channel; runs the instrument's table) ----------
4668 SoundProcessChannelTable   ; advance/apply the channel's table (wChannelTable/Played/Countdown); calls the column readers
574B SoundReadTableEnvelope     ; read table_envelopes[wChannelTable][row] (song $1690 = SRAM bank0 $B690)
587D SoundReadTableTranspose    ; read table_transposes[wChannelTable][row] (song $3480 = SRAM bank1 $B480)
487E SoundReadGroove            ; -> e = grooves[wChannelGroove][wChannelGrooveRow] (song $1090 = SRAM bank0 $B090) via wPointerGroove/wPointerGrooveRow
; --- Sequencer: song row -> chain -> phrase resolution ------------------------
48D2 SoundAdvanceSongRow        ; on wChannelChain[ch]==$FF, walk chain_assignments (loop-back) -> next chain
5EAD SoundReadSongChain         ; e = chain_assignments[wChannelSongRow[ch]][ch] ($B290 = song offset $1290)
5E7C SoundReadChainPhrase       ; e = CHAIN_PHRASES[wChannelChain[ch]*16 + wChannelChainRow] (SRAM bank1 $A080) -> wChannelPhrase
; --- Per-tick FX command dispatch (command value in a -> CommandHandlers) -------
; Command values index the same table as the mnemonics at $0824 ("-ABCDEFGH...").
; B/D/G/H have null handlers here -- they act at note-trigger, not per tick.
4790 SoundDispatchCommand       ; a = command value (<19); jp CommandHandlers[a]
47A2 CommandHandlers            ; [19] dw: each command's per-tick handler (FxCmd_*; 0 = none)
4679 Command_A                  ; A: table start/stop
476C Command_C                  ; C: chord
46D8 Command_E                  ; E: amplitude envelope
46F7 Command_F                  ; F: wave frame / finetune
4812 Command_S                  ; S: sweep / shape
47C8 Command_W                  ; W: wave / duty cycle
4286 Command_L                  ; L: slide (legato)
69D7 EnvelopeReleaseSpeeds      ; [8] envelope fade speed per release digit (SoundEnvelopeReleaseSpeed)
6246 Command_M                  ; M: master volume
665F Command_O                  ; O: output (panning)
6646 Command_P                  ; P: pitch bend / shift
45D8 SoundApplyPitchBend        ; Command_P tonal-channel impl: set up pitch bend from hCommandValue (per-chan accum wChannelPitchTarget)
43D8 PitchBendTable             ; [256] UWORD exponential pitch curve; SoundApplyPitchBend reads [$43D8 + 2*hCommandValue]
6669 Command_T                  ; T: tempo
649D Command_R                  ; R: retrig
65F3 Command_K                  ; K: kill note
7DD1 Command_V                  ; V: vibrato
7D81 VibratoDepthTable          ; [16] vibrato depth curve, Command_V reads [VibratoDepthTable + (hCommandValue & $0f)]
7D91 VibratoRateTableA          ; [16] UWORD vibrato rate (type A); [$7D91 + 2*(hCommandValue>>4)]
7DB1 VibratoRateTableB          ; [16] UWORD vibrato rate (type B); selected by wChannelVibratoType
7EAC KitPitchTable              ; [120] per-pitch kit sample step deltas (SoundSetKitParameters)

; --- context-based names (named for the role their callees show) ---
4000 SoundCommandParsePitchValue ; parse an FX value (mask $80/$0f) -> SoundInitializeEnvelope
4033 SoundKitStepLoopWindow1    ; kit S cmd, voice 1: the high digit shifts the loop window (+/- digit*16, each edge clamped to the sample), the low digit moves its end (kept $10 past the start), then the read pointer is rewound into the window; Command_S runs SoundKitStepLoopWindow2 next
40E6 SoundClampKit1LoopEnd      ; clamp wKit1LoopEnd down to wKit1SampleEnd: a = 0 if it was past it, else 1
410C SoundClampKit1LoopStart    ; clamp wKit1LoopStart up to wKit1SampleStart: a = 0 if it was below it, else 1
4132 SoundKeepKit1LoopOpen      ; keep kit voice 1's loop window open: if wKit1LoopEnd is not past wKit1LoopStart, set it to wKit1LoopStart + $10
4154 SoundKitStepLoopWindow2    ; kit S cmd, voice 2: SoundKitStepLoopWindow1's twin over wKit2Loop*/wKit2ReadPointer (both call the other voice's start clamp: the ROM's cross-wiring)
4208 SoundClampKit2LoopEnd      ; clamp wKit2LoopEnd down to wKit2SampleEnd: a = 0 if it was past it, else 1
422E SoundClampKit2LoopStart    ; clamp wKit2LoopStart up to wKit2SampleStart: a = 0 if it was below it, else 1
4254 SoundKeepKit2LoopOpen      ; keep kit voice 2's loop window open: if wKit2LoopEnd is not past wKit2LoopStart, set it to wKit2LoopStart + $10
4276 SoundDivideWithRemainder   ; 16-bit hl / 8-bit c -> quotient in l, remainder in a (shift-subtract)
43CE SoundCommandTableJump      ; FX dispatch via computed jump (jp hl region)
4637 SoundClampNoteRange        ; clamp a note value to playable range ($3c..$78) -> wChannelDisplayNoteNoi
46C7 SoundClearChannelCommandSlots ; clear this channel's 3 FX slots (wChannelCommandSlots/$c2f4/$c2f8 + ch)
472F SoundRunTableColumn        ; b picks the slots: bit 0 runs the command slot's countdown ($C230 + wCommandChannel; at 0 SoundRunCommandSlot), then the retrig slot's ($C23C +, SoundRetrigNote) only with bit 1; bit 0 clear runs the retrig slot alone
4753 SoundRunChannelCommandSlots ; iterate the 12-entry FX-slot table wChannelCommandSlots, run SoundRunTableColumn per active
478D SoundDispatchStoredCommand ; load command from wCommand, fall into SoundDispatchCommand
483F SoundAdvanceTableCursor    ; advance this channel's table read cursor (wPointerPhraseRow ptr + wChannelInstrumentPointer[ch])
48AB SoundAdvanceGroove         ; step the channel's groove row (wrap 15 / skip zero-tick), reload the note tick countdown
4B8A SoundReadChainTranspose    ; read chain_transposes[wChannelChain[ch]] from SRAM bank1 ($A880, di/ei guarded) -> per-channel shadow wChannelChainTranspose[ch]
4BC5 SoundTransposeNote         ; add chain transpose (wChannelChainTranspose, song/chain mode) + global transpose to the note; skip if wChannelTranspose set
4C26 AdvanceCurrentChannelCursors ; set de=hSoundChannel*2, c=a (amount), then fall into SoundAdvanceChannelCursors (advance current channel's cursors by a)
4C42 SoundAnyChannelActive      ; -> e = 0 when none of the 8 wChannelActive flags ($C0E0..7) is set, else nonzero (8 minus the first set one's index); also nz/z, with a the flag
4C4E SoundStartChannel          ; handle wChannelRestart (re)start request: read seq (SoundStartChannelFromRow), set retrigger wPlayRestartPending, clear request
4C68 SoundLoadChannelInstrument ; read the channel's instrument number from SRAM bank3 via its wChannelInstrumentPointer[ch] cursor -> wChannelInstrument shadow (wChannelActiveInstrument/$c210[ch]); then SoundLoadInstrument
4C9C SoundReadChainRow          ; read the current chain row (cp $ff = end-of-chain)
4CBF SoundAdvanceChainRow       ; advance the chain row, load that row's phrase; end-of-chain handling at row 16/$ff
4D71 SoundStepAllChannels       ; run SoundProcessChannel (sequencer step: advance phrase, read note/cmd) for each active channel, order WAV,PU1,PU2,NOI
4DA9 SoundEnterSongRow          ; commit wChannelNextSongRow -> wChannelSongRow, load its chain ($ff -> scan up)
4E17 SoundMaskLow5              ; return a & $1f
4E2A SoundStepTableHopCount     ; Hxy with a count (the column, 0 or 1, and xy on the stack): this channel's hop counter for the column (wTableHopCounters) starts at x and counts down a hop at a time to row y (SoundTableHop, -> e its result); spent, e = 0 (no hop) and it rests at $FF for the next time
4E69 SoundQueueSyncByte         ; store a byte to $cbdc / wSyncTransmitByte (sync transmit)
4E74 SoundDeactivateChannel     ; clear wChannelActive[ch] and wChannelRestart[ch] (stop this channel)
4EA3 SoundResetCommandState     ; clear retrigger wPlayRestartPending, wSoundTick, wSpeechWord, wPlayMinutes
4F2B FillChannel16              ; write a to the 16 bytes from hl, -> hl past them (a staggered entry into the FillChannel8/4 unrolled memset)
4F2F FillChannel12              ; write a to the 12 bytes from hl, -> hl past them (a staggered entry into the FillChannel8/4 unrolled memset)
4F3C SoundDecodeCommandNibbles  ; decode a command's nibbles ($01/$02 cases)
4FC0 SoundApplyTableCommand     ; (cp $02) SoundReadSramByteVia then jp SoundClampNoteRange
503C SoundReadSramByteVia       ; hl -> a pointer: -> e = the SRAM byte it points at ($0A enable, di/reti)
504A SoundRunTableStep          ; run a table step (SoundDecodeCommandNibbles, SoundNoiChordStep)
5074 SoundRandom15              ; -> e = randw() % 15: B (MayBe) in a phrase plays when this is below the probability digit
507F SoundAdvanceStatePointers  ; advance the 7 working sound-state pointers (low bytes wPointerChainRow/e1/e3/e5/e7/eb/ed) to the next channel's slot in the $C1xx tables (counterpart of SoundInitializeStatePointers)
509C SoundReadPhraseCommand     ; -> e = the current row's phrase command (0 none; SRAM bank 2 phrase_fx), kept with its value for the channel; H/W special-cased
50E1 SoundReadTableCommand1     ; -> e = the table's CMD1-column command (0 none) via the wTableCommand1Pointer/wTableCommand1ValuePointer stream pointers, kept with its value for the channel
5119 SoundReadTableCommand2     ; -> e = the table's CMD2-column command (0 none) via the wTableCommand2Pointer/wTableCommand2ValuePointer stream pointers, kept with its value for the channel
5165 SoundReadCommandStream     ; read command-stream bytes (wSoundDataStride; cp $ff = end)
5345 SoundSetupWaveChannel      ; ch2 (WAV/KIT): seed working ptrs (wPointerStepCountdown/e3/e5/e7/fc), SoundReadCommandStream
5459 SoundReadCursorByte        ; read a byte via wPhraseCommandPointer[ch] cursor + wPointerNoteSource (SRAM-guarded)
5477 SoundTableHop              ; hop this channel's table to row a & $0F: the transpose and left command columns, or with bit 7 the right command column (its own row); e = 0 if already there
54D7 SoundUpdateAllChannels     ; output phase of a tick: for each active channel (wChannelActive $C0E0..7) set hSoundChannel and call SoundUpdateChannel (writes sound regs / runs tables)
556A SoundRunFrame              ; per-frame sound entry (called from main loop, bank00 $2317): tempo gate -- if wFrameSkip pending skip it; else run SoundTick 1+wTickRepeat times this frame
5583 SoundApplyTableTranspose   ; jp target from SoundStepTablePointers: read table_transpose row, add to the channel note, apply (SoundTableHop)
55AE SoundCountdownStep         ; count down this channel's ticks left in the step: e = 0 if idle; at 0, flag the note trigger and advance the groove
55CB SoundNoteDue               ; -> e = nonzero, with wChannelNoteTrigger[ch] set too, when the channel's note countdown ([wPointerNoteCountdown]) is 0 and it is not held for a live start (wLiveStartColumn is $FF, or wPlayRestartPending); else e = 0
55EF SoundTableCommand1Hop      ; table command column 1's H: H0y hops to row y (SoundTableHop), Hxy counts x hops first (SoundStepTableHopCount); -> e = 0 when it did not hop
5604 SoundTableCommand2Hop      ; table command column 2's H: as SoundTableCommand1Hop for the right column (bit 7 to SoundTableHop); -> e = 0 when it did not hop
561B SoundAdvanceTableRow       ; advance the channel's table one row when it runs per tick (wChannelTableStep 0): its five read pointers (note, two commands, two values) step on; skipped the tick a table starts (wChannelTableFresh, cleared here; NOI also clears wNoiTableNotePrevious)
5657 SoundStepTablePointers     ; advance the channel's table step counter; on 16-step wrap rebuild SRAM read-pointers ($c1xx) for the table transpose ($B480) and command ($BA80) columns of wChannelTable[ch]
56E1 SoundReadGrooveValue       ; table step 0 -> jp SoundAdvanceGroove unless the groove byte is $20; step 8 -> mark it $ff. (The trailing .initEnvPu1/.initEnvNoi stubs, zeroing wEnvelopeStagePu1/Noi = ex-$cbbf, are separate entries.)
572B SoundInitializeEnvelope    ; init 3-node envelope for hSoundChannel channel (WAV: none); stage=0, node1 -> vol+speed
5778 SoundSetKitParameters      ; set kit state wWavSynthFrame/wWavRamDirty/wWavSynthEnd
583F SoundSplitPhraseNibbles    ; wChannelPhrase[ch] -> hi/lo nibbles (compute phrase index)
58C7 SoundFillFF                ; write $FF to the 32 bytes from hl (-> hl past them, a = $FF)
58EA SoundLoadInstrument        ; copy the 16-byte instrument record instruments[a] (SRAM bank1 $B080+a*16) into wCurrentInstrument ($C0D0)
5F5E SoundResetChannelCommand   ; reset this channel's (hSoundChannel) retrigger rate, pitch slide and vibrato, and its LFO
5FA7 SoundResetWavCommand       ; the WAV channel's part of SoundResetChannelCommand (retrigger, update flags, pitch rate, frame delta, vibrato)
5FBE SoundResetWavFlat          ; SoundResetWavCommand, then a flat wave ($77 x 16) in hWavUploadBuffer
5FDA SoundSetChannelEnable      ; enable/disable this channel in rAUDENA (per hSoundChannel; SoundWritePanning)
61A9 SoundWritePanning          ; a & 3 = the channel's output (the O command): set this channel's panning bits in rAUDTERM (wChannelOutputOverride when its bit 7 is set)
61F7 SoundClearVoiceHram        ; clear $ffa0-$ffa3 (per-voice HRAM shadow regs)
6270 Command_P_Step             ; P with PITCH on STEP: the pitch changes at once (a kit's rate by 3 a step, else wChannelPitchCurrent by 8)
632B Command_F_Wav              ; F on the wave channel: a synth's wave frame steps; a kit's two sample positions move (x16, doubled beyond +-16)
6479 SoundRandomUpTo            ; random 0..n (randw() % (n + 1); 0 for 0): the range Z adds to each digit
6577 SoundKillNote              ; kill this channel's note (K, now or when its slot's timer runs out): FX and FX slots, pitch slide, chord, vibrato off, table $FF
6685 SoundRunCommandSlot        ; set hSoundChannel = wCommandChannel & 3, run SoundKillNote
6694 SoundWavLevelStep          ; step the WAV output level (NR32 bits 5-6) by the signed high digit of the argument: negative towards off, positive towards 100%
66E7 SoundRetrigNote            ; R fires: play the slot's channel's latest note again (slide, envelope, table restarted), then reload or end the slot
68A0 SoundNoiPitchStep          ; the noise channel's pitch each tick: P's slide in quarter semitones, then V's offset, as note steps
6904 SoundNoiChordStep          ; step the noise channel's chord (C): the note, the first digit's offset, the second's (skipped when 0), the note again; SoundClampNoteRange gets the change
69C3 SoundEnvelopeReleaseSpeed  ; E's release digit (hCommandValue & 7) -> the envelope fade speed (EnvelopeReleaseSpeeds)
69DF SoundEnvelopeReleaseTarget ; E's release direction (the second digit's bit 3, 9-F fade up): the volume the envelope fades toward, $0F or 0
69F2 Command_E_Pu1              ; E on PU1 (from Command_E): restart the envelope (retriggering when the length bit is set), then fade at SoundEnvelopeReleaseSpeed toward SoundEnvelopeReleaseTarget
6A28 Command_E_Pu2              ; E on PU2, as Command_E_Pu1
6A5E Command_E_Noi              ; E on NOI, as Command_E_Pu1
6A94 SoundLiveQueueStart        ; live mode: queue channel (arg) to start the song row's chain when its current one ends; again on the same row (chain/phrase screen) start at the edited chain row, sooner; with a sync restart pending, start now
6B59 SoundSetPlayRange          ; the channels to play (wPlayChannelFirst..Last): the song cursor's column, or on the song screen in selection mode the selection's columns
6B9B SoundLiveQueueRange        ; live mode: queue a start for each channel in the play range (SoundLiveQueueStart)
6BBA SoundStartChannelFromRow   ; start this channel playing from wChannelNextSongRow ($ff -> stop path)
6D97 SoundStartChannels         ; start channels [wPlayChannelFirst..wPlayChanLast] from wSongRow (per-screen playback entry)
6E0F SoundStartRange            ; start the play range: queued behind what is playing if any channel is active (SoundLiveQueueRange), else at once (SoundStartChannels)
6E24 SoundLiveStopRange         ; live mode, stop the play range's channels (SELECT+START): queued starts cancelled; an active channel stops at its chain's end, or its phrase's when pressed again (wChannelLiveQueued)
6EA7 SoundLiveStartQueued       ; live mode: a channel queued to start (wChannelLiveQueued) whose chain has ended starts now (wChannelRestart)
6F65 SoundGetChainPhrase        ; bounds-checked chain_phrases[chain*16+row] lookup (chain=arg sp+6, row=arg sp+7 <$10; SRAM $A080); DebugTrap on out-of-range
6FB6 SoundStepWavFrames         ; step the synth's frames: on the timer, add the delta list's next step to wWavSynthFrame and reload the wave; at the list's end stop (play mode 1) or loop
7034 SoundSpeechStep            ; speech: when the frame's ticks run out, play the word's next allophone (SRAM bank 0 stream at wSpeechPointer; 0 ends the word) on kit voice 2, then read the next frame's length
70FB SoundEnableLcdInterrupts   ; SetInterruptEnable
710E SoundInitializePlayState   ; copy wCurrentScreen -> wPlayMode, clear wLiveMode, SoundTogglePlayback
711F SoundPhraseHop             ; H in a phrase: HFF stops the song; else, once a tick, go to the low digit's row of this phrase (after the high digit's count of hops) or, playing a chain or the song, of the chain's next phrase; e = 0 no hop, 2 stopped, 1 hopped
7362 SoundTableMaybeHop         ; B in a table (MayBe hop): with the high digit's probability (/16), hop to the low digit's row (arg: the right command column); e = 1 if it hopped
73B0 SoundZRepeat               ; Z for a command slot (slot, last): repeat the last command that was not Z or H (wLastCommand[last]) with wLastCommandValue[last] + 0..each Z digit; e = the command
743E SoundZPhrase               ; Z in a phrase (tail-jumped from SoundReadPhraseCommand): SoundZRepeat(hSoundChannel, hSoundChannel)
744D SoundZTableCommand1        ; Z in a table's CMD1 column: SoundZRepeat(4, 4 + the channel's table)
746F SoundZTableCommand2        ; Z in a table's CMD2 column: SoundZRepeat(5, $24 + the channel's table)
748E SoundReadChannelStep       ; read the channel's next step: its note (or the PS/2 keyboard's), the groove's ticks less any D delay owed, its instrument (or the keyboard's), then the transpose (a kit note on WAV is masked instead)
75C6 SoundUpdateChannel         ; per-channel processor (channel = hSoundChannel): advance phrase cursor, resolve song/chain row, read note/cmd; called per active channel by SoundUpdateAllChannels
77F0 SoundTick                  ; one engine tick: SoundStepAllChannels (sequencer) then SoundUpdateAllChannels (output); self-recurses on retrigger flag wPlayRestartPending / mode wSyncMode
786F SoundLiveChainEnd          ; live mode, at a chain's end: stop the channel if wChannelStopQueued (the sound too once none plays), else start its queued song row (SoundEnterSongRow); e = 1 if neither
792B SoundStartSongPlayback     ; start the song, all four channels, at the song cursor's row: each channel's chain there, walking back past empty rows; from another screen's chain row (SELECT+START, sync OFF or KEYBD) each chain starts at that row, modulo its length
7B31 SoundStartScreenPlayback   ; start the current screen's playback: the song from the cursor row (SoundStartSongPlayback), or the edited channel's chain or phrase
7C4C SoundTogglePlayback        ; START: stop all playback, then start the current screen's unless it was the one playing (sync stop otherwise); live mode: SoundStartRange
7CFB Command_E_NoteOn           ; E at a note-on (SoundNoteToPeriod): PU1/PU2/NOI stop the fade, the first digit sets wChannelEnvelope (e = 5: the release runs); WAV sets wWavLevel (e = 0)
7F24 SoundSetupLfo              ; dispatch by hSoundChannel -> SoundSetupLfoPu1/PU2/WavNoi (vibrato/LFO setup)
7F33 SoundSetupLfoWavNoi        ; LFO setup for ch2/3 (WAV/NOI): e = the target volume; clear wEnvelopeStageNoi, hl = wChannelEnvelopeNoi, c = rAUD4ENV, then SoundStepEnvelopeToTarget
7F3E SoundSetupLfoPu2           ; LFO setup for ch1 (PU2): e = the target volume; clear wEnvelopeStagePu2, hl = wChannelEnvelopePu2, c = rAUD2ENV, then SoundStepEnvelopeToTarget
7F49 SoundSetupLfoPu1           ; LFO setup for ch0 (PU1): a = the stage (wEnvelopeStagePu1), e = the target volume; hl = wChannelEnvelope, c = rAUD1ENV, then SoundStepEnvelopeToTarget
78C4 SoundToggleSongPlayback    ; SELECT+START on any screen: SoundTogglePlayback as if on the song screen (all four channels); live mode: SoundLiveStopRange
5EDA NoiseFrequencyTable        ; [120] NR43 poly/divisor byte per noise note
5F52 SoundSetNoisePolynomial    ; a = the noise note: rAUD4POLY (NR43) = NoiseFrequencyTable[a]; -> hl at the entry (SoundClampNoteRange keeps h)
7F51 SoundStepEnvelopeToTarget  ; step the channel volume at hl toward e via zombie mode ($08 nudge up / SoundFadeEnvelopeStepDown); c = rAUDxENV; shared tail of SoundSetupLfo*
7F5C .stepDown                  ; target below current: fade one step down (SoundFadeEnvelopeStepDown)

